-- K12's simulator: the list of the test on G_u at a run, at the maker's return, past SaysAt.
/-
AtFullSide/K12/OnAtRunUPaid.lean: CONDITIONAL: A CONDITIONAL WITH NO KNOWN MEMBER.

Can the hypotheses be met together at a real run? NOT KNOWN. G with hP: a term lies at this G's own
type: `theGAtBase` with `theGAtBase_prover` (E2E/TheG.lean; not imported): its
prover at the return's prover is the return's; BUT its two arguments, the threads' parts and the
kinds' rows, have no known value. The list, a value of `ThreadsP`, ready's and runC's return and
that the part is called have no term and no law known to us: where the part is never called the ends
hold for nothing. hB: under the head the library's maker of books returns
(`bookWhole_returns_at_head_ahead`, AtFullSide/K14/WholeAheadAtHead.lean); that the rule's book Bk
is that book is asked in the first statement and paid in the second. hAns: see below.

What is here. `onAtRun_U_at_return` (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K12/Sim2/ListU.lean) WITH ITS
CLAUSE ON VALUES `SaysAt`, ASKED AT EVERY STAND AND ALL CARRIED COINS, AND ITS TWO TESTS ON THE
BOOK, GIVEN UP FOR TWO PREMISES: hB (the book is the library's) and hAns. In the side library,
because the law that it calls is: `onFreeT_head_U_paid` (AtFullSide/K12/OnFreeTAtHeadUPaid.lean),
which ends in the whole condition `OnFreeT` under ∃ ca m with BOTH ties (carriedAt … = .ok ca at the
run's own coins, and the walk's own equation for m): so the rule's ca and m are these, and the end
is `OnAtRun₂` itself. No definition; two statements.

  `onAtRun_U_at_return_paid`   the statement, at any book that the library's maker of books returns
      (hB).
  `onAtRun_U_at_the_returns_book`   the same at the book that the maker returns with the prover: hB
      is paid (`atPure_book_at_head`, Honest/K14/AtPureBookAtHead.lean; `made_sends_at_files`,
      Honest/K14/SharedSendsWritten.lean): among the binders no premise on a book is left. The
      book's return has moved into hAr: what is won is which book, not that the maker of books
      returns; it stands at the list of merges that the maker guesses (that file's own words).

THE PREMISES, SORTED. PUBLIC: h · hb. THE MAKER: hAr. THE BOOK: hB. THE RUN: T · hρ · hR · hrun: the
rule's own letters; the proofs read nothing of T. WHICH OBJECTS: hP · hA · hJs (it pins all four
fields of the simulators' job: the place's numbers, that the first fold sends no table of its own,
the state function, the trees named) · hL. THE FILLING. At W₀ := the matrices, I := `matrixInput`,
S' := Sz.ref, O := openHonest, `onlineProverPartsInUse I secondHashFunction S' O` is `baseFilling` by its text
(E2E/BaseMaker.lean). Two things are not shown here or beneath: that the own test's rows are ready,
and that the lent o_sp words are tied at the tests on G_u and on G_omega through `OnlineProverParts.through`.
The wide filling is defined in Honest/K1/Law/WSideAtFill.lean. This file does not show that the
maker returns at it. THE ONE
CLAUSE ON VALUES: hAns : `OwnAnswers` (Johnson/Desc/K14/Honest/ItemsEach.lean) at the instance's key
x.pub.key and at the rows as the two senders are handed them (`heldAt` of `askOf` at ⟨w₀, rc,
x.pub.key⟩: by `ready_ok` and hα that is the input that ready lays for the shared chain, at every
k). To its text: for each seed of the key and each row, a sum over the row's plain places and three
of its pads equals the key's recorded answer. IT READS THE INDEX, THE COMMITTER's PADS AND THE KEY;
IT NAMES NO COIN k THAT THE BOOK LENDS, NO CHALLENGE, NO STAND AND NO CARRIED BLOCK: so where it
holds of (w₀, rc, x) it holds at every k and every due list of challenges of that (w₀, rc, x). The
row's own order of binders, for whoever states "at every coin": every (w₀, rc, x) of the relation,
every k, every return, one T, then every due list of challenges outside the silent set, every run.
"At all csU, csO" costs nothing: `OwnAnswers` reads the rows alone; the ∀ is the called law's form
and is idle. It follows from "the instance's key is the committer's make at this index and this
randomness" (`answers_held`, Honest/K12/HeldAtCommitter.lean); it is weaker: it speaks of the
answers in the key's record against the rows, and says nothing on the seeds' form, the key's sizes
or the item; no relation is named here. At a key without seeds it is met for lack of a case; the
committer's key is no such key: at the full size it has one seed, and there hAns is 2^11 equations.

A LIMIT ON THE COMMITTER's RANDOMNESS, BEFORE THE OTHERS (Johnson/Bind/ForProver/FiveAt.lean's head,
"A limit on the coins"), SAID HERE OF hAns: at a fixed index and key the pads that the answers read
are fixed, wherever no seed has the factor 0. AT THE FULL SIZE THESE ARE ALL PADS OF EVERY ROW (one
seed, three pads a row): the tails alone stay free. That index and key fix the pads is reckoned by
hand off the texts there; no theorem says it. THESE STATEMENTS STAND AT SINGLE VALUES: w₀, rc and x
are bound together, and there a seed may be a letter bound beside them. NO LATER LAW MAY RANGE OVER
rc WITH THE INSTANCE's KEY A LETTER UNDER SUCH A PREMISE AND SPEAK OF THE PADS AS UNIFORM: it would
range over one point in them. In a law over the committer's randomness the key is written as the
term made of index, randomness and seed, and the seed as the term made of index and randomness. No
strategy or simulator may branch on "the key is the committer's": it reads index and pads.

What the proof pays besides ListU's: hα (the parts' key is the instance's): `key_at_pure` · hst (the
prover's stored table is the committer's, at this index and this randomness): `atPure_storedWords` ·
hgS (the eighth sub-protocol's half is what the search finds): by the filling's own shared list
(`sixBody_at_head`, `halves_eq`, `places4`, `facts_at_head`) · hT, hbk: inside the law called, from
hB.

STAND-INS BENEATH [a reader's list, held against the proofs by reading]: the filling's shared list
is empty where the six other sides' maker errs · `halfU` is empty where the job is not made · the
kind K14's halves are three where the shape does not split · `doorUF`'s fall-back state · `heldAt`'s
total moves (a coin beyond an array is 0; a default shape) · a record too short is read as 0 · the
copy's number beside the seed is read by nothing. NO PAYMENT HERE HOLDS BECAUSE OF ONE: the first
three are shut out by laws under the head; the others are read by no premise that these proofs pay,
or make hAns harder, not free.

OF WHAT KIND THE LAW CALLED IS (its own head's words): three of the laws that it calls, on the
fields coin and tie and on the clause trees, "are ties between what one part is handed of a run's
values and what another part is handed of them". "The job's first member carries no vector of its
own; one reader of the index serves the test, the two senders and "SPLIT"." "It moves no count."

Through its imports this file stands over files under Johnson/Goal/ (a walk of the import lines).





Limits. All limits of Sim2/ListU.lean's and AtFullSide/K12/OnFreeTAtHeadUPaid.lean's heads. The rule
moves the debt and pays none of it; this file does pay: it brings the debt at one list down to hAns.
No later law may take the condition On as a hypothesis on a run and then speak of the random values
as sampled anew. Rows stay at the filling's types: no crossing to the online prover is typed
here. Nothing on completeness, soundness or hiding.
No property is claimed.
-/
import AtFullSide.K12.OnFreeTAtHeadUPaid
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2.ListU
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K14.PaidAt
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K14.PartsPlay
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K14.AtPureBookAtHead
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K14.SharedSendsWritten

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace AtFullSide.K12
open OnBytes (E TableKey)
open VerifiableInference.Desc (Block Chain)
open VerifiableInference.Desc (K1.qAt)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.First (S)
open Johnson.G (codesFull2 proofSendsFull)
open Desc.K14 (St blocks)
open Desc.K14.Honest (OwnAnswers)
open ProofFile.Honest ProofFile.Honest.K12 ProofFile.Honest.K12.Light ProofFile.Honest.K12.AtProof ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2
